  <issue>
  Fading Module: Removing the clutter
## Enhancement proposal
At the moment, the animation.fading module contains 10 Animation clsses:

`FadeIn`, `FadeInFrom`, `FadeInFromLarge`, `FadeInFromPoint`, `VFadeIn`, `FadeOut`, `FadeOutAndShift`, `FadeOutToPoint`, `VFadeInThenOut`, `VFadeOut`

I think `FadeIn` and `FadeOut` is enough. Let me explain:
Basically there are 3 distinctions: Direction(In or Out), Movement (shift, specific position, None) and Scaling (grow, shrink, None)
FadeIn and FadeOut need three new parameters:
`FadeIn(..., scaling=1, shift=None, from_position=None)` and `FadeOut(..., to_position=None)`

This doesn't only reduce the clutter of too many classes, it also shows a lot more clearly, what the Animation actually does:
```
Direction   Scaling     Shifting    Animation
In          shrink      shift       
Out         shrink      shift       
In          grow        shift       
Out         grow        shift       
In          -           shift       FadeInFrom
Out         -           shift       FadeOutAndShift
In          shrink      position    
Out         shrink      position    
In          grow        position    FadeInFromPoint
Out         grow        position    
In          -           position    
Out         -           position    FadeOutToPoint
In          shrink      -           
Out         shrink      -           
In          grow        -           FadeInFromLarge
Out         grow        -           
In          -           -           FadeIn
Out         -           -           FadeOut
```

Why are `FadeInFrom` and `FadeOutAndShift` named so differently? Why does `FadeInFromPoint` scale the Mobject but `FadeOutToPoint` doesn't? Why are there these specific classes, but others not (a personal favorite would be `FadeOutAndShrinkToPointWhileShifting` :smile: )?

And about the `VFade...` Animations (they are supposed to be used for VMobjects, who knew?): They should simply be deprecated, they have no use as far as I can tell.

Since two classes would be a bit lonely in their own module, I would like to let them join the other creation animations :slightly_smiling_face: 



## Additional comments
100 points go to the person naming the remaining 11 Animations :laughing:
